# Cloudflare Pages response headers for apps/web's bundle.
#
# Copied into apps/web/dist at deploy time (wrangler.toml says why it is not in
# apps/web/public/). Pages reads this file from the root of the deployed directory.
#
# There is deliberately no Content-Security-Policy here. CesiumJS creates web workers and
# instantiates WebAssembly from its own static directory, and a policy written without a
# browser to test it against is a policy that breaks the globe on first load and looks
# like a Cesium bug. Add one when someone can watch the console while it is applied.
#
# There is also no _redirects file. The bundle is three real HTML entry points, not a
# single-page app with client-side routing: the phone handoff opens `/upload.html#token`
# verbatim (app/services/captures.py) and the console is `/admin.html`. A catch-all
# `/* /index.html 200` would turn every typo into a silently-served globe instead of a
# 404, and would buy nothing.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Vite's output: content-hashed filenames, so a stale copy is unreachable by name.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# CesiumJS's static build directories (workers, WebAssembly, star and moon textures).
# vite.config.ts copies them under a path named for the installed `cesium` version,
# CESIUM_BASE_URL = `/cesium/<version>/` (`/cesium/1.145.0/` today), so upgrading the
# dependency changes every URL instead of the contents behind one. That is what makes
# `immutable` safe here: a returning browser can never pair last year's workers with this
# year's engine, because this year's engine asks for different names. They used to sit at a
# fixed `/cesium/` with a day's lifetime, which re-validated 40-odd files on the first visit
# of every day. Nothing else is served under /cesium/. (The version alone names the contents
# because `Build/Cesium` ships prebuilt in the npm package; the pnpm patch only touches
# @cesium/engine's sources. A patch to the `cesium` package itself would have to change the
# name too.)
/cesium/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted fonts (apps/web/public/fonts) and their licences. The file names carry the
# upstream release (`-v4-`, `-v21-`), and a new cut of a font gets a new name, so these are as
# immutable as the hashed bundle.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The entry documents name the hashed assets, so they must not be cached past a deploy.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
